\section{Every row lands with \code{ein_b} NULL, and that is the source's shape}{

The file gives \verb{(527 EIN) -> (ENTITY_NAME, address)}. There is no counterparty
EIN anywhere in it. Resolving a name to an EIN is a \emph{matching} problem and
belongs to \code{npmatch}, so these rows record the counterparty by name and leave
\code{ein_b} open. \code{PLAN.md} §4 made \code{ein_b} nullable for exactly this source.

The gap is not small and pretending otherwise would mislead a consumer: of
10,597 distinct counterparty names, \strong{1,564 (14.8\%) exactly match a BMF legal
name}. The rest are sponsoring corporations, unions and trade associations
that are largely outside the exempt universe altogether. A consumer treating
\code{related_name} as resolvable should expect roughly one in seven to resolve.
}

